From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:38:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 124/159] ASoC: qcom: sm8250: Capture ports follow the FE

The backend fixup forces every DAI to 2 channels. For the codec DMA
and VA capture ports this means the uplink of a voice call runs in
stereo while the DSP voice processor is set up for a single channel
(as Qualcomm's own driver does for a single-microphone call): on the
Moto G 5G Plus, calls with the q6voice driver were then silent in both
directions.

Leave the channel count of the TX and VA codec DMA ports to the front
end, so that a mono voice uplink runs the port in mono and a stereo
recording still gets both microphones. Playback ports keep 2
channels.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
index 5866f1f34b3d..8a61c5a9fce9 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
@@ -63,11 +63,30 @@ static int sm8250_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 	struct snd_interval *channels = hw_param_interval(params,
 					SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_CHANNELS);
 	struct snd_mask *fmt = hw_param_mask(params, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_FORMAT);
+	struct snd_soc_dai *cpu_dai = snd_soc_rtd_to_cpu(rtd, 0);
 
 	rate->min = rate->max = 48000;
-	channels->min = channels->max = 2;
 	snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
 
+	/*
+	 * Codec capture ports follow the front end: the voice uplink is mono
+	 * (that is what the DSP voice processor is told), a recording may be
+	 * stereo.
+	 */
+	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
+	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_0:
+	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_1:
+	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_2:
+	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_3:
+	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_4:
+	case TX_CODEC_DMA_TX_5:
+	case VA_CODEC_DMA_TX_0 ... VA_CODEC_DMA_TX_2:
+		break;
+	default:
+		channels->min = channels->max = 2;
+		break;
+	}
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
